#![enable(implicit_some)]

[
(
    act: 0,
    sub: 0,
    location: "any",
    id: "player_death",
    messages: [
        (
            id: "judgment",
            text: "A cold shiver crawls down your spine as darkness closes in. Flesh, ambition, and memory fade alike, reduced at last to ash. Every dream you carried loses its meaning before the silence of the afterlife. There is nothing left now but to face your particular judgment.",
        ),
        (
            id: "cadet",
            text: "Your orders end here, Cadet. The world will continue without your answer, your ambitions unfinished and your questions unresolved. Whatever comes next, you face it alone.",
        ),
        (
            id: "it_hurts",
            text: "It... hurts...   ...   ..  .             .              ",
        ),
    ],
    next: None,
),
(
    act: 1,
    sub: 1,
    location: "start",
    id: "act1_001.introductory_text",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: "In 2010, the world tore open.

            Rifts opened across Earth, and creatures emerged from whatever lay beyond them. Humanity gave that place many names. Tartarus was the one that stuck.

            In the span of 3 years, some regions were effectively lost:
            Siberia,
            parts of Northern Canada
            Lake Chad,
            Bosnia,
            Baluchistan,
            and the worst humanitarian catastrophe of the new age - the island of Java.

            The damage went far beyond the land that was lost. Governments collapsed, borders moved, and wars that had lasted generations ended overnight only for new ones to begin.

            Across much of the world, emergency powers became permanent and tyrannical regimes arose as frightened populations learned to accept the new reality.

            Only scattered pockets of freedom and democracy remained, places where fragments of the old order were still preserved.

            Brazil survived the first great rift in the Amazon. Its soldiers fought until they had reclaimed enough ground to build a wall and contain what remained beyond it.

            From that war came the Lenhadores - soldiers remade into something stronger than the men they had once been.

            The rifts also brought something humanity had never seen before: a strange mineral found where the world had been wounded. It was precious, dangerous, and, against the creatures of Tartarus, indispensable.

            Then came the second rift, six times larger.

            It consumed much of the Paraíba Valley and drove millions toward the coast and São Paulo. City after city was evacuated as the defensive line collapsed westward.

            The wall was finally set at Guarulhos and for a time, São Paulo stood almost empty beneath the shadow of the Second Wall.

            The nation survived, but the Republic that had entered 2010 did not. In the decades that followed, Brazil rebuilt itself around the walls, the Lenhadores, and the resources drawn from the wounds left by the rifts.

            Forty-three years later, the walls still stand, smaller rifts still open, and the Lenhadores still guard what lies beyond them.

            Brazil is now an Empire.

            Ten years ago, your father, one of those soldiers himself, crossed one of those walls.
            He never came back.

            It is the year 2053, and today, Cadet, you report for Lenhador induction.
            ",
        ),
    ],
    next: Some("act1_002.arrival"),
),

// ENLISTMENT LINE

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.arrival",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: "Goiânia, July 6th 2053
            It's winter. Though in the midwest there are only two seasons: hot and dry (winter and autumn), and hot and wet (summer and spring). You feel your throat dry up under the sun while the shade of a cloud is the only comfort.

            Ahead of you is a long intake line. Everyone is holding documents or keeping them close, each with their respective suitcase holding minimal clothes. All waiting for the moment they will be asked for them. Some hold their folders in both hands, like plates. Others keep checking the same bag pocket that hasn't changed since the last check. Some brought food: box juice, cereal bars. Others didn't even bring a water bottle or a cap to protect from the sun.

            White T-shirts, white sneakers, blue jeans. The standard cotton swab loadout, as it's called in the armed forces. Some candidates already shaved their heads; others clearly held onto their hair until the last possible day.

            A few eventually sit on the floor. The line moves so slowly that standing for three or four hours accomplishes nothing.

            A slightly uneasy candidate stands immediately in front of you. Looking like a cotton swab, like everyone else, though his brown quill hairstyle stands out and, in a way, denounces his partial commitment to letting go of his past life. He's white, yellowish-green eyes, perhaps of southern or uruguayan descent. You heard that uruguayans born past 2030 are able to become Lenhadores. He holds a thick, transparent folder containing forms, documents and medical exams.

            You begin to feel your legs a bit tired from all the waiting.
            ",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                The line advances another few meters, then stops again.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                Every candidate ahead of you is holding some subset of the same documents.

                The important-looking ones are easy to recognize.

                IMPERIAL ARMY - VOLUNTARY ENLISTMENT - FORM 3-B
                IMPERIAL LENHADOR CORPS - VOLUNTARY ENLISTMENT - FORM 33-A
                CADET ADMISSION AND INCORPORATION DECLARATION - FORM 3-C
                DECLARATION OF INTENT TO ENTER ACTIVE IMPERIAL SERVICE - FORM 3-D
                DECLARATION OF PRIOR MILITARY SERVICE - FORM 6-A
                DECLARATION OF CIVIL AND DEPENDENT STATUS - FORM 8-C
                AUTHORIZATION FOR BACKGROUND AND SERVICE RECORD REVIEW - FORM 11-F
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                Then come the documents proving that you are, in fact, yourself.

                NATIONAL ID OF THE EMPIRE OF BRAZIL
                Individual Taxpayer Registry Certificate
                Birth Certificate
                Certificate of Imperial Citizenship
                Certificate of Registered Domicile
                Proof of Current Residence

                Then the documents proving that you went to school.

                Secondary School Completion Certificate
                Secondary School Academic Transcript
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                Somewhere ahead, a candidate slides his transcript out, looks at it, and files it back two documents deeper.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                Then the documents proving that, as far as several different offices are concerned, you have not done anything that would prevent you from being here.

                Certificate of Civic Regularity
                Certificate of Military Service Status
                Certificate of Discharge or Reservist Status
                Imperial Military Justice - Negative Record Certificate
                Provincial Civil Justice - Negative Record Certificate
                Declaration of Moral Suitability for Imperial Service
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                And then there is the medical file.

                PERSONAL AND FAMILY MEDICAL HISTORY - FORM MED-1
                DECLARATION OF FITNESS FOR MILITARY TRAINING — FORM MED-2
                Vaccination Record
                Complete Blood Count
                Blood Type and Rh Factor
                Coagulation Profile
                Fasting Blood Glucose
                Urea and Creatinine
                Hepatic Function Panel
                Urinalysis
                Stool Parasitology
                Syphilis Serology
                HIV Serology
                Hepatitis B Serology
                Hepatitis C Serology
                Toxicological Screening
                Chest Radiographs - PA and lateral
                Cervical, Thoracic and Lumbar Spine Radiographs
                Resting Electrocardiogram
                Exercise Stress Test
                Pure-Tone and Speech Audiometry
                Complete Ophthalmological Examination
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                A girl two places up holds her chest radiograph at arm's length against the light. The plastic has gone warm and slightly soft in the sun.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                That would already be enough paperwork for most branches of the Army.

                You volunteered for the Lenhadores.

                LENHADOR CANDIDATE MEDICAL DISCLOSURE - FORM 33-B
                GENETIC COMPATIBILITY CERTIFICATE - LC-GEN/4
                METAMORPHIC COMPATIBILITY PANEL - LC-MCP/2
                BASELINE NEUROCOGNITIVE ASSESSMENT - LC-NC/7
                MINERAL SENSITIVITY AND REACTIVITY ASSAY - LC-MR/3
                DECLARATION OF PRIOR ABYSSAL EXPOSURE - FORM 33-E
                CONTAMINATION AND ANOMALOUS EXPOSURE SCREENING CERTIFICATE - LC-AE/5
                DECLARATION OF PRIOR USE OF CONTROLLED METAMORPHIC AGENTS - FORM 33-F
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                And, finally, some medical forms.

                INFORMED CONSENT FOR METAMORPHIC INDUCTION - FORM 33-C
                ACKNOWLEDGEMENT OF IRREVERSIBLE PHYSIOLOGICAL ALTERATION - FORM 33-C/II
                ACKNOWLEDGEMENT OF LONG-TERM MEDICAL MONITORING REQUIREMENTS - FORM 33-C/IV
                AUTHORIZATION FOR RETENTION OF BIOLOGICAL SAMPLES - FORM 33-G
                DESIGNATION OF NEXT OF KIN - FORM 33-H
                DESIGNATION FOR RELEASE OF PERSONAL EFFECTS - FORM 33-H/II
                DECLARATION CONCERNING RECOVERY AND DISPOSITION OF REMAINS - FORM 33-H/III
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                Most keep that last one somewhere in the middle of the stack, stapled to Next of Kin, face down.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                Getting all of it here was an ordeal in itself, and quite expensive. From the acceptance notice to reporting day, you had a month.

                Most candidates did not bother keeping the entire stack in their hands. Documents they were reasonably sure nobody would ask for remained inside their suitcases.

                Reasonably sure.

                Every few minutes, someone farther ahead in the line starts digging frantically through a bag.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                Six candidates cleared the desk in the last twenty minutes.

                There are forty-odd ahead of you.

                The line doesn't advance continuously. It stalls for long stretches, then compresses four or five people at once.

                You can harvest some comfort, and tell that nervous-looking candidate ahead of you that you came up with a plan to rest your legs a bit.
            "#,

            when: [
                AttributeAtLeast(
                    attribute: Reasoning,
                    value: 2,
                ),
            ],
        ),
    ],

    choices: [
        (
            id: "sit",
            text: "<Sit down.>",

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetSatInLine),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.line_settles",
        ),

        (
            id: "stand",
            text: "<Stay standing.>",

            next: "act1_002.line_settles",
        ),

        (
            id: "reasoning_tell_tomas",
            text: "\"It stalls, then it jumps. Sit when it stops moving, stand when it compresses. We will manage to keep our place and rest our legs this way.\"",

            when: [
                AttributeAtLeast(
                    attribute: Reasoning,
                    value: 2,
                ),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetGaveTomasPracticalAdvice),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.line_advice",
        ),
    ],

    next: None,
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.line_settles",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                You sit against the wall with the others.
            "#,

            when: [
                Flag(CadetSatInLine),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                You stay on your feet.

                It doesn't make the line move any faster.
            "#,

            when: [
                Not(
                    Flag(CadetSatInLine),
                ),
            ],
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.signature"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.line_advice",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Hmm, I was thinking about that\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He looks toward the front of the line, does some arithmetic of his own, then lowers himself against the wall without letting go of his folder.
            "#,
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.signature"),
),

// The signature

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.signature",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                At the front of the slow-moving line, a kid seems to be in trouble. He's shaking.

                The recruiter handling him isn't much older. Khaki fatigues, sleeves rolled up against the heat, a cheap fan rattling beside the desk.

                Behind him, taped to the wall, a laminated portrait of the Emperor has gathered a bit of dust, but keeps an eye on the future Lenhadores.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Recruiter"),
            text: "\"The signature looks different from the one in your ID.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Nervous Candidate"),
            text: "\"Sorry. Please, just let it pass. I signed it fast. Look at the photo. It's me.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Recruiter"),
            text: "\"Should've signed it slower. Go to the end of the line. We'll decide what to do with you when this is over.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He isn't angry with the kid.

                He's enjoying how nervous he is, and the way every objection immediately turns into an apology.
            "#,

            when: [
                SkillAtLeast(
                    skill: Empathy,
                    value: 20,
                )
            ],
            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetReadRecruiterCorrectly),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He doesn't mark the form, separate it from the others, or look at the ID again before waving the kid away.

                This isn't cadre making an enlistment decision. He's a recent recruit on intake duty, bottom of the food chain. Once you are sworn in you will outrank him.

                If the signature were grounds for rejecting a candidate, someone with real authority would have to be called.

                He hasn't called anyone.
            "#,

            when: [
                SkillAtLeast(
                    skill: MilitaryAffairs,
                    value: 20,
                ),
                Not(
                    AttributeAtLeast(
                        attribute: Reasoning,
                        value: 3,
                    ),
                ),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetReadRecruiterCorrectly),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                Sending him to the back of the line instead of escalating it tells you the recruiter doesn't intend to make much of this.

                Once everyone else is processed, turning it into a real problem means finding a superior, explaining it, and creating work for himself.

                The recruiter will just stamp the form.
            "#,

            when: [
                AttributeAtLeast(
                    attribute: Reasoning,
                    value: 3,
                ),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetReadRecruiterCorrectly),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                The kid walks past the line without looking at anyone. The next candidate is already putting his papers on the desk.

                After a few minutes, once everything is stamped, the recruiter pulls a laminated card from under the desk and reads off it without looking down.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Recruiter"),
            text: "\"Do you enter this service of your own will, owing loyalty to the Empire before family, faith and self.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                It clearly isn't a question. The candidate's face is clearly serious as he says yes.

                Stamp. Next.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: "The candidate next to you feels compelled to speak.",
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Lost half the day because he couldn't sign his own name. The Empire doesn't need clumsy soldiers who can't even follow the public notice properly.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"At least that's one less ahead of us.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"...That sounded meaner out loud.\"",
        ),
    ],

    choices: [
        (
            id: "agree",
            text: "\"You're not wrong.\"",

            effects: [
                SetTomasFirstImpression(Warm),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.signature_agree",
        ),

        (
            id: "callout",
            text: "\"You enjoyed saying that.\"",

            effects: [
                SetTomasFirstImpression(Teasing),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.signature_callout",
        ),

        (
            id: "confront",
            text: "\"Could've happened to you.\"",

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetChallengedTomas),
                SetTomasFirstImpression(Blunt),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.signature_confront",
        ),

        (
            id: "vulnerable",
            text: "\"Could've happened to me.\"",

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetSharedVulnerabilityWithTomas),
                SetTomasFirstImpression(Warm),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.signature_vulnerable",
        ),
        (
            id: "authority",
            text: "\"It's clearly the same guy. They have his picture. Those milicos are just being assholes. It's what they call the Little Power Syndrome, right?\"",

            when: [
                Not(
                    Flag(CadetReadRecruiterCorrectly),
                ),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetOpenlyQuestionedAuthority),
                SetTomasFirstImpression(Blunt),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.signature_authority",
        ),

        (
            id: "authority_read",
            text: "\"He'll let him through, eventually. The recruiter just wants to make him wait and savour his moments of authority. Milicos are petty tyrants who enjoy every inch of power they get\"",

            when: [
                Flag(CadetReadRecruiterCorrectly),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetOpenlyQuestionedAuthority),
                SetFlag(CadetPredictedRecruiterOutcome),
                SetTomasFirstImpression(Blunt),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.signature_prediction",
        ),

        (
            id: "silent",
            text: "<Say nothing.>",

            effects: [
                SetTomasFirstImpression(Distant),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.signature_silent",
        ),
    ],

    next: None,
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.signature_agree",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He seems relieved that somebody let it pass.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Right? It's a long day. You get mean.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He goes back to watching the desk.
            "#,
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.tomas_turn"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.signature_callout",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"...Yeah. A little.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He doesn't argue with it. He looks toward the front of the line for a while.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Long day.\"",
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.tomas_turn"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.signature_confront",
    messages: [
                (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                The joke dies in his mouth.
            "#,
        ),
        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"It couldn't, really. I checked mine four times.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He tightens his grip on the folder as he says it, which undermines the point a bit.
            "#,
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.tomas_turn"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.signature_vulnerable",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He looks at you properly for the first time.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Could've happened to anyone, you mean.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He thinks about it.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Yeah. That's the part that gets me. It isn't about being good enough. It's whoever's behind the desk.\"",
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.tomas_turn"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.signature_authority",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: "You said that a bit louder than you wanted to. Good thing no one listened. Questioning authority in public could cause you trouble.",
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Keep your voice down.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He looks at the desk. Then at the portrait behind it.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"You're not wrong. And they're the ones holding your paperwork.\"",
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.tomas_turn"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.signature_prediction",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: "You said that a bit louder than you wanted to. Good thing no one listened. Questioning authority in public could cause you trouble.",
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Keep your voice down.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He looks at the desk anyway.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"We'll see.\"",
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.tomas_turn"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.signature_silent",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                You don't give him anything.

                He waits a few seconds, then pretends he was talking to himself.
            "#,
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.tomas_turn"),
),

// Tomas at the desk

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.tomas_turn",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                The candidate beside you reaches the desk eventually.

                His preparation borders on absurd.

                Forms. Copies. Medical exams. Identification. Copies of the identification. Copies of documents that probably didn't need copies.

                Everything is arranged inside a thick transparent folder.

                He still looks nervous.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Recruiter"),
            text: "\"Fitness declaration.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                The candidate reacts immediately.

                He pulls out a sheet and hands it over.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Recruiter"),
            text: "\"That's not what I asked for.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He takes the paper back.

                Now one hand is holding the folder, another is holding the rejected sheet, and somehow he needs a third to search through everything else.

                The neat stack begins to collapse.

                A tab divider slips loose. He pins the folder against his hip with an elbow. The rejected sheet is creasing in his grip and he notices, and stops, and can't do anything about it.

                Behind him, forty people are watching him fail at something he prepared days for. It's the overpreparation that's the most humiliating.
            "#,
        ),


        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                You remember seeing him reorganize the folder earlier.

                He put the fitness declaration immediately beneath the X-ray paperwork.
            "#,

            when: [
                AttributeAtLeast(
                    attribute: Memory,
                    value: 3,
                ),
            ],
        ),
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                The fitness declaration is visible about halfway through the stack. Its header is printed in a different typeface from the medical forms around it. It's between the X-ray paperwork and a yellow form.
            "#,

            when: [
                AttributeAtLeast(
                    attribute: Perception,
                    value: 3,
                ),
            ],
        ),
    ],

    choices: [
        (
            id: "perception_help",
            text: "<Whisper> \"Above the yellow form.\"",

            when: [
                AttributeAtLeast(
                    attribute: Perception,
                    value: 2,
                ),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetHelpedTomasAtIntake),
                SetFlag(TomasNoticedCadetObservant),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.tomas_discreet_help",
        ),

        (
            id: "memory_help",
            text: "<Whisper> \"You put it under the X-ray.\"",

            when: [
                AttributeAtLeast(
                    attribute: Memory,
                    value: 2,
                ),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetHelpedTomasAtIntake),
                SetFlag(TomasNoticedCadetMemory),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.tomas_discreet_help",
        ),

        (
            id: "help_search",
            text: "<Help him search through the documents.>",

            when: [
                Not(
                    AttributeAtLeast(
                        attribute: Agility,
                        value: 2,
                    ),
                ),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetHelpedTomasAtIntake),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.tomas_help_search",
        ),

        (
            id: "help_search_agility",
            text: "<Steady the stack and pull the declaration free.>",

            when: [
                AttributeAtLeast(
                    attribute: Agility,
                    value: 2,
                ),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetHelpedTomasAtIntake),
                SetFlag(TomasNoticedCadetQuickHands),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.tomas_help_agility",
        ),

        (
            id: "help_deception",
            text: "<Lie> \"The major said the fitness declaration goes in tomorrow, at the first PT exam. Have you been stamping them all morning without need?\"",

            when: [
                SkillAtLeast(
                    skill: Deception,
                    value: 30,
                ),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetHelpedTomasAtIntake),
                SetFlag(TomasNoticedCadetDeceptive),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.tomas_help_deception",
        ),

        (
            id: "public_defense",
            text: "\"He's got it. Give him a second.\"",

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetHelpedTomasAtIntake),
                SetFlag(CadetPubliclyDefendedTomas),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.tomas_public_defense",
        ),

        (
            id: "one_less",
            text: "\"Tick-tock. Careful or it'll be one less.\"",

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetThrewOneLessBackAtTomas),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.tomas_one_less",
        ),

        (
            id: "do_nothing",
            text: "<Do nothing.>",

            next: "act1_002.tomas_finds_it",
        ),
    ],

    next: None,
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.tomas_finds_it",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He almost drops the entire folder before finding the form himself.

                The recruiter takes it without comment.
            "#,
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.after_tomas_turn"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.tomas_one_less",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Fuck you.\"",

            when: [
                Any([
                    TomasFirstImpression(Warm),
                    TomasFirstImpression(Teasing),
                ]),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                Despite himself, he laughs.

                It makes searching considerably harder.
            "#,

            when: [
                Any([
                    TomasFirstImpression(Warm),
                    TomasFirstImpression(Teasing),
                ]),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Very funny.\"",

            when: [
                Any([
                    TomasFirstImpression(Blunt),
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ]),
            ],
        ),
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He doesn't laugh.

                He finds the form on his own, and doesn't look at you again until the recruiter has stamped it.
            "#,

            when: [
                Any([
                    TomasFirstImpression(Blunt),
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ]),
            ],
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.after_tomas_turn"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.tomas_discreet_help",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                His eyes follow yours.

                He pulls the correct form free.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Got it.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                A few seconds later, without quite looking at you:
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Thanks.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He squares the edges of the stack. Squares them again.
            "#,
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.after_tomas_turn"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.tomas_help_search",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                You take part of the stack before it spills.

                Between the two of you, you find the declaration.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Thanks.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He takes the rest of the stack back out of your hands fast.
            "#,
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.after_tomas_turn"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.tomas_help_agility",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                The folder starts to fold open.

                You catch the loose stack against his forearm before anything hits the floor, spot the declaration as the papers separate, and slide it free.
            "#,
        ),
        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"...Okay. Thanks.\"",
        ),


        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He takes the papers back.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"...Thanks.\"",
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.after_tomas_turn"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.tomas_help_deception",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                You say it flatly, the way you'd repeat something boring that everyone already knows.

                The recruiter stops. Looks at the morning's stamped stack sitting in its tray. Forty forms, every one with a fitness declaration behind it.

                Checking means asking someone. Asking someone means saying, in front of the whole line, that he might have been doing it wrong since eight.

                He scratches his head. Looks at the portrait on the wall.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Recruiter"),
            text: "\"...Tomorrow. Fine.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Recruiter"),
            text: "\"Do you enter this service of your own will, owing loyalty...
            Alright, [STAMP] next!
            \"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He waves the candidate through and calls the next one. You.

                It isn't until he's past the barrier that the candidate looks at you, thinking to himself.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"...I don't recall the major saying anything like that.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Did he...?\"",
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.after_tomas_turn"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "enlistment_line",
    id: "act1_002.tomas_public_defense",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: Some("Recruiter"),
            text: "\"Did I ask you?\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                The candidate's expression tightens.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"I have it.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He finds the declaration and hands it over.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Thanks. But I had it.\"",
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.after_tomas_turn"),
),
(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "intake_yard",
    id: "act1_002.after_tomas_turn",

    on_enter: [
        (
            when: [
                TomasFirstImpression(Blunt),
                Flag(CadetHelpedTomasAtIntake),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetTomasFirstImpression(Teasing),
            ],
        ),

        (
            when: [
                TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                Flag(CadetHelpedTomasAtIntake),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetTomasFirstImpression(Blunt),
            ],
        ),
        (
            when: [
                TomasFirstImpression(Blunt),
                Flag(CadetThrewOneLessBackAtTomas),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetTomasFirstImpression(Distant),
            ],
        ),

        (
            when: [
                TomasFirstImpression(Teasing),
                Flag(CadetThrewOneLessBackAtTomas),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetTomasFirstImpression(Blunt),
            ],
        ),

        (
            when: [
                TomasFirstImpression(Warm),
                Flag(CadetThrewOneLessBackAtTomas),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetTomasFirstImpression(Teasing),
            ],
        ),
    ],

    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                Then it's you.

                Your papers go onto the desk. The recruiter pulls the ID out from under your fingers before you've let go of it. Pages turn. Forms leave your stack, get flattened, get stamped, and start a second stack facing the other way.

                He holds the ID up. Half a second on the photo. Half a second on your face. Down.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Recruiter"),
            text: "\"Do you enter this service of your own will, owing loyalty to the Empire before family, faith and self.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                The card is laminated. The sentence has no question mark anywhere in it.

                You say yes.

                Stamp. Next.
            "#,
        ),

        // Distant: no scene.
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He's already halfway across the yard, folder under his arm, walking toward the shade with everyone else.
            "#,

            when: [
                TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He's past the barrier, standing off to the side with the folder under his arm.
            "#,

            when: [
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Avelar.\"",

            when: [
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He adjusts the folder under his arm.
            "#,

            when: [
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Candidate"),
            text: "\"Tomás.\"",

            when: [
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"That thing back there. I'd have found it.\"",

            when: [
                Flag(CadetPubliclyDefendedTomas),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"But thanks. I know how it looked.\"",

            when: [
                Flag(CadetPubliclyDefendedTomas),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"Still thinking about what you said. About it happening to me.\"",

            when: [
                Flag(CadetChallengedTomas),
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"It wouldn't have.\"",

            when: [
                Flag(CadetChallengedTomas),
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He watches the line for a while. It hasn't gotten shorter.
            "#,

            when: [
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"So why'd you sign up?\"",

            when: [
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
            ],
        ),
    ],

    choices: [
        (
            id: "father",
            text: "\"My father was a Lenhador. Went over a wall ten years ago. Never came back.\"",

            when: [
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetMentionedFather),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.after_father",
        ),

        (
            id: "practical",
            text: "\"Money. Same as everyone else in this line.\"",

            when: [
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.after_practical",
        ),

        (
            id: "deflect",
            text: "\"You first.\"",

            when: [
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.after_deflect",
        ),

        (
            id: "silent",
            text: "<Say nothing.>",

            when: [
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.after_silent",
        ),

        (
            id: "offend",
            text: "\"Ask me again when you can hold a folder.\"",

            when: [
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetOffendedTomas),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.after_offend",
        ),

        (
            id: "keep_walking",
            text: "<Head for the shade.>",

            when: [
                TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.arrival_end",
        ),
    ],

    next: None,
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "intake_yard",
    id: "act1_002.after_father",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He looks at you.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"Oh.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                A few seconds.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"Right.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"That's a good reason. Sorry you went through that.\"",
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.arrival_end"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "intake_yard",
    id: "act1_002.after_practical",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"Honest, at least.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"Everyone ahead of us has a speech ready. You'll hear about forty of them this week.\"",
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.arrival_end"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "intake_yard",
    id: "act1_002.after_deflect",

    on_enter: [
        (
            effects: [
                SetFlag(TomasGaveHisReason),
            ],
        ),
    ],

    messages: [
        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"Money.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He answers before you finish asking.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"Pay's stupid for someone my age. And the pension goes to family, if it goes wrong.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                That one was ready. So are the other two, lined up behind it: security, service. He picked the one that needed the least explaining.
            "#,

            when: [
                SkillAtLeast(
                    skill: Empathy,
                    value: 20,
                ),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He waits.
            "#,
        ),
    ],

    choices: [
        (
            id: "father",
            text: "\"My father was a Lenhador. Went over a wall ten years ago. Never came back.\"",

            effects: [
                SetFlag(CadetMentionedFather),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.after_father",
        ),

        (
            id: "practical",
            text: "\"Same. Money.\"",

            next: "act1_002.after_practical",
        ),

        (
            id: "silent",
            text: "<Say nothing.>",

            next: "act1_002.after_silent",
        ),
    ],

    next: None,
),

// Reached from two places: before he answered, and after. He is owed a
// reply in the second case and merely ignored in the first.
(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "intake_yard",
    id: "act1_002.after_silent",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He waits to see whether anything else is coming. Nothing is.
            "#,

            when: [
                Not(
                    Flag(TomasGaveHisReason),
                ),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"Fair. It's a stupid question to ask on the first day.\"",

            when: [
                Not(
                    Flag(TomasGaveHisReason),
                ),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"Right.\"",

            when: [
                Flag(TomasGaveHisReason),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He gave you his. He doesn't ask again.
            "#,

            when: [
                Flag(TomasGaveHisReason),
            ],
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.arrival_end"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "intake_yard",
    id: "act1_002.after_offend",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"Right.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                Whatever his face was doing a moment ago, it stops. He adjusts the folder under his arm and doesn't answer.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"Good luck in there.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He walks off toward the shade.
            "#,
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.arrival_end"),
),

// CLOSING

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "intake_yard",
    id: "act1_002.arrival_end",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                Behind you, the nervous candidate is back at the desk.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                The recruiter glances at the signature again.

                He sighs.

                Stamp.

                The kid is waved through.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"You called it.\"",

            when: [
                Flag(CadetPredictedRecruiterOutcome),
                Not(
                    Flag(CadetOffendedTomas),
                ),
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                The kid passes you on his way to the yard.
            "#,

            when: [
                Flag(CadetOpenlyQuestionedAuthority),
            ],
        ),
    ],

    on_enter: [
        (
            when: [
                Flag(CadetPredictedRecruiterOutcome),
                Not(
                    Flag(CadetOffendedTomas),
                ),
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
            ],

            effects: [
                SetFlag(TomasRespectsCadetJudgment),
            ],
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.barracks_assignment"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "barracks_214",
    id: "act1_002.barracks_assignment",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                The rest of the day is more lines.

                A line for a wristband. A line for a bedding roll. The same instructions repeated at every station, word for word, to each group of ten.

                The water in your bottle has been warm since noon. The last cereal bars come out of bags. Candidates shift their folders from one hand to the other, then back. The shade you watched all morning crosses the yard and ends up against the far wall.

                Near evening, names are called in groups of four.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("NCO"),
            text: "\"Avelar, Tomás.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("NCO"),
            text: "\"[PLAYER_NAME]\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("NCO"),
            text: "\"Silva, Rafael.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("NCO"),
            text: "\"Siqueira, Nadja. Room 214.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                Avelar, Tomás. The candidate from the line is in your group.
            "#,

            when: [
                Any([
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                    Flag(CadetOffendedTomas),
                ]),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                The candidate from the line looks over at you.
            "#,

            when: [
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
                Not(
                    Flag(CadetOffendedTomas),
                ),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"No fucking way.\"",

            when: [
                Not(
                    TomasFirstImpression(Distant),
                ),
                Not(
                    Flag(CadetOffendedTomas),
                ),
            ],
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                Room 214 is small and functional.

                Four lockers, doors ajar, keys hanging in the locks. Two bunk beds, mattresses still in plastic. One window, painted shut, looking onto the yard you spent the day in. The room smells of floor wax and, under it, faintly, of whoever lived here before.

                Bare walls, except for the same laminated portrait, issued one to a room.

                Boots and voices move down the corridor. Doors keep opening in the same rhythm, four names at a time.

                Names have already been taped to the bedframes. Typed, cut into strips.

                Tomás reads them.

                Then reads them again.

                You and Tomás have been assigned the same bunk.
            "#,
        ),

        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"You've got to be kidding me.\"",

            when: [
                Not(
                    Flag(CadetOffendedTomas),
                ),
            ],
        ),
    ],

    choices: [
        (
            id: "claim_top",
            text: "\"Top bunk's mine.\"",

            next: "act1_002.barracks_claim_top",
        ),

        (
            id: "offer_choice",
            text: "\"You care which one you get?\"",

            next: "act1_002.barracks_offer_choice",
        ),

        (
            id: "could_be_worse",
            text: "\"Could've been worse.\"",

            when: [
                Not(
                    Flag(CadetOffendedTomas),
                ),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.barracks_could_be_worse",
        ),

        (
            id: "one_less_callback",
            text: "\"One less would've been nice.\"",

            when: [
                Flag(CadetThrewOneLessBackAtTomas),
            ],

            next: "act1_002.barracks_one_less",
        ),

        (
            id: "silent",
            text: "<Drop your bag beside the bunk.>",

            next: "act1_002.barracks_silent",
        ),
    ],

    next: None,
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "barracks_214",
    id: "act1_002.barracks_claim_top",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"By all means.\"",
        ),

        (
            speaker: None,
            text: r#"
                He takes the bottom. Starts unpacking.
            "#,
        ),
    ],

    next: Some("act1_002.barracks_close"),
),

(
    act: 1,
    sub: 2,
    location: "barracks_214",
    id: "act1_002.barracks_offer_choice",
    messages: [
        (
            speaker: Some("Tomás"),
            text: "\"Bottom. I get up early and I'd rather not do it from a ladder.\"",

            when: [
